# MadGraph5 batch script: g g > t t~ QCD<=2
# in SMEFTsim_topU3l_MwScheme (UFO v3.0.2), restricted by restrict_SMlimit_massless.dat.
#
# Why this exact process:
#   The same SM-limit process as gg_to_ttx_smlimit with the coupling order
#   written out. It is the control on MadGraph's default WEIGHTED bound: the
#   model carries an effective ggH vertex at SMHLOOP = 1, whose g g > H > t t~
#   diagram the default bound drops and an explicit QCD<=2 keeps. The two rows
#   therefore differ by exactly that one diagram, which is what makes the
#   default's effect a measured number rather than an inference.
#
# The model path is repo-relative to the vendored UFO; build.sh rewrites it to
# the work-area copy it stages under output/models/, which is where the
# vg_* restrict cards of validation/madgraph/cards/smeft/ are placed. Both
# generators therefore prune vertices from the same card.
#
# `display interactions` prints the count MadGraph's own interaction splitting
# arrives at (one interaction per coupling-order tuple, import_ufo.add_interaction)
# into the build log, which is where extract_interactions.py reads it from.
import model validation/ufo/SMEFTsim_topU3l_MwScheme_UFO-SMlimit_massless
display interactions
generate g g > t t~ QCD<=2
output gg_to_ttx_smlimit_qcd2 -nojpeg
launch
set lpp1 0
set lpp2 0
set ebeam1 250
set ebeam2 250
set use_syst False
done
